  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-cumpuncta-melak-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<p>From the Betta unimaculata complex. IUCN Red List: N/A. Wild-caught Betta compuncta from Melak.</p><ul><li>Maximum size: 3+ inches</li><li>TDS: ~60–100</li><li>pH: ~5.0–7.0</li><li>Temperature: 72–82°F (prefers cooler temperatures, but higher temperatures induce coloration and breeding behaviour)</li><li>Breeding: Mouthbrooder</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-cumpuncta-melak-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<p>Carnivorous. Fed on live, frozen and dried foods, such as blackworms, frozen bloodworms and pellets.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-cumpuncta-melak-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<p>Like many species in this complex, the largest bettas can be aggressive. They are best kept in a species-only tank, as they can eat anything that fits in their big mouth.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-cumpuncta-melak-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<p>Light brown to tan base body with light blue iridescence on the opercular cheeks and lower jaws, body and tails; females have less iridescence. Fully grown adult males have longer ventral fins and larger bodies.</p>"
    }
  ],
